arameter> are the string. They must","-    satisfy the same constraints as described for the","-    <literal>s</literal> type in","+    <para>In case of <function>sd_bus_message_append_string_memfd()</function>, the contents of","+    <parameter>memfd</parameter> starting at the specified <parameter>offset</parameter> and of the specified","+    <parameter>size</parameter> are used as the string. <parameter>size</parameter> must include the","+    terminating <constant>NUL</constant> byte, i.e. the resulting string has length","+    <parameter>size</parameter> - 1. If <parameter>offset</parameter> is zero and <parameter>size</parameter>","+    is <constant>UINT64_MAX</constant>, the full contents of the memory file descriptor are used, and hence","+    must themselves end in a <constant>NUL</constant> byte. If <parameter>offset</parameter> plus","+    <parameter>size</parameter> exceeds the actual size of the memory file descriptor, this call fails with","+    <constant>-EMSGSIZE</constant>. The memory file descriptor is sealed by this call if it has not been","+    sealed yet, and cannot be modified after this call. The appended contents must satisfy the same","+    constraints as described for the <literal>s</literal> type in","     <citerefentry><refentrytitle>sd_bus_message_append_basic</refentrytitle><manvolnum>3</manvolnum></citerefentry>.</para>"," ","     <para>In case of","@@ -89,7 +97,7 @@","     similar to <function>sd_bus_message_append_basic()</function> with","     type <literal>s</literal>, but instead of copying a string into","     the message, it returns a pointer to the destination area to","-    the caller in pointer <parameter>p</parameter>. Space for the string","+    the caller in pointer <parameter>ret</parameter>. Space for the string","     of length <parameter>size</parameter> plus the terminating","     <constant>NUL</constant> is allocated.</para>","   </refsect1>"],"additions":15,"deletions":7,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/basic/memfd-util.c","lines":["@@ -96,10 +96,27 @@ int memfd_get_sealed(int fd) {","         if (r < 0)","                 return r;"," ","-        /* We ignore F_SEAL_EXEC here to support older kernels. */","+        /* We ignore F_SEAL_EXEC here to support older kernels.","+         * It is supported since kernel v6.3 (6fd7353829cafc4067aad9eea0dc95da67e7df16). */","         return FLAGS_SET(seals, F_SEAL_SHRINK | F_SEAL_GROW | F_SEAL_WRITE);"," }"," ","+int memfd_set_sealed_gracefully(int fd) {","+        int r;","+","+        r = memfd_set_sealed(fd);","+        if (r != -EPERM)","+                return r;","+","+        /* Already sealed? Check if required seals are set. */","+        r = memfd_get_sealed(fd);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return r;","+        if (r == 0)","+                return -EPERM; /* Propagate the original error. */","+        return 0;","+}","+"," int memfd_get_size(int fd, uint64_t *ret) {","         struct stat stat;"," "],"additions":18,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/basic/memfd-util.h","lines":["@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@ static inline int memfd_new_and_seal_string(const char *name, const char *s) {"," "," int memfd_set_sealed(int fd);"," int memfd_get_sealed(int fd);","+int memfd_set_sealed_gracefully(int fd);"," "," int memfd_get_size(int fd, uint64_t *ret);"," int memfd_set_size(int fd, uint64_t sz);"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/fuzz/fuzz-bootspec.c","lines":["@@ -112,7 +112,7 @@ int LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput(const uint8_t *data, size_t size) {","         if (getenv_bool(\"SYSTEMD_FUZZ_OUTPUT\") <= 0) {","                 orig_stdout_fd = fcntl(fileno(stdout), F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC, 3);","                 if (orig_stdout_fd < 0)","-                        log_warning_errno(orig_stdout_fd, \"Failed to duplicate fd 1: %m\");","+                        log_warning_errno(errno, \"Failed to duplicate fd 1, ignoring: %m\");","                 else","                         assert_se(freopen(\"/dev/null\"